      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a Zephyr config. Using it outside of the `/zephyr` directory is a layer violation.\n\nI understand your intention. The constants `CONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_OFF` and `CONFIG_EC_WRITABLE_STORAGE_OFF` come from the `binman`\u0027s `wp_ro` and `ec-rw` nodes. I saw the following CL defined the `binman` node. You might shift the CL order.\n\nAnd the constants `CONFIG_RO_STORAGE_OFF` and `CONFIG_RW_STORAGE_OFF` are chip specific, and the RTK chip should have its own values, which should be defined in the Zephyr shim layer, i.e. `zephyr/shim/chip/`.",
